/doc/helpdir/mail
=================

SYNTAX
======

mail - loads your mail reader
checkmail - checks to see if you have mail
readmail- puts you into the mail system (see arguments below)
closemail - removes your reader

mail <person> (only works if you have a mail reader loaded) - sends
mail to another character.

Using the "set" command, you can set your mud mail to be forwarded
to your internet email address.  See "help set" for more information.

The following commands are issued from the mail prompt.
(1-max_num)   Show that message number
.             Show the current message again
+             Show the next message
+<number>     Show the message <number> ahead of this one
-             Show the previous message
-<number>     Show the message <number> before this one
d <number>    Delete message <number> from your mail.
h             Show message headers
l             Save the current message to /log/<you>.mbox
n             Goto and show next message
R             Reply to the current message's sender
r             Reply to the current message's sender and Cc's
      q             Quit mail
      x             Quit mail without erasing any messages
      ?             Show this help information

DESCRIPTION
===========

Send/read mail to/from someone else in the mud.

